### Chart 1A: Boundary Deferral, Gated Hold & Tool-Boundary Pause

| Evidence Field | Required Finding |
| --- | --- |
| **SSPS reference** | **Mint-to Logic™** (April 15, 2025 formal stage drawings, Stage `[400]` Routing Decision Layer & Stage `[500b]` Limbo conditional hold / escalation / expiration branch) and **The Shepherd's Method™ / Process** (December 19, 2024 provisional filing baseline — continuous pre-execution pacing and boundary deferral). |
| **External product** | **NVIDIA Dynamo v1.6.0** (builtin `ThunderAgent` plugin `#15164`, `RequestClassifier` `#14123`, and `DispatchGate` `#14177`) & **Amazon Bedrock AgentCore Policy / Gateway** (Cedar threshold-gated escalation rules). |
| **Input** | **Dynamo v1.6.0:** Normalized HTTP/gRPC inference requests carrying session headers (`X-Dynamo-Session-ID`, `parent_session_id`, `nvext.agent_hints`) and turn triggers (`user_message` vs. `tool_result`). **AgentCore Gateway:** MCP `tools/list` and `tools/call` payloads enriched with JWT/IdP identity claims (`sub`, group claims) and tool parameters. |
| **Validation** | **Dynamo v1.6.0:** `RequestClassifier` (`classify`) assigns lane keys/policy classes and validates worker pins, reservations, and capacity; `DispatchGate` (`check`) evaluates lane head-of-line readiness and waiting budget; `ThunderAgent` evaluates KV pool utilization bands (`0.80` soft-demote, `0.95` pause, `0.85` resume hysteresis). **AgentCore Policy:** Default-deny Cedar RBAC/ABAC rules (`permit` / `forbid`) evaluate principal identity, environment tags, and parameter thresholds prior to backend invocation. |
| **State artifact** | **Dynamo v1.6.0:** Lane-queued request state (`Hold` vs. `Go` with `until` deadline), session-to-block lineage index (`#13807`), and paused program marker at tool boundary. **AgentCore:** Isolated runtime microVM session (up to 8 hours) with scoped Cognito/JWT session context and `approvalStatus` policy evaluation attribute. |
| **Routing** | **Dynamo v1.6.0:** Deadline-ordered policy queue (`#14176`) and unified worker selection (`#14570`, `--router-policy-config` `#15202`) scoring KV prefix overlap, active load, and priority hints. **AgentCore Gateway:** Ordered request interceptors and Cedar policy evaluation dispatch approved calls to registered MCP targets or block/escalate threshold-exceeding calls. |
| **Execution** | **Dynamo v1.6.0:** Dispatches admitted LLM turns to GPU inference workers while pausing/deferring new turns at tool boundaries under KV pressure (subject to a forced-resume cap); external tool execution remains in the caller's agent harness. **AgentCore:** Executes approved tool calls via MCP targets and runs code/shell actions inside isolated microVM sandboxes (Strands Shell). |
| **Terminal behavior** | **Dynamo v1.6.0:** Ordered lifecycle events (`Sent`, `Responding`, `Completed`, `Aborted`) release tracked request and scheduler state on completion, rejection, or cancellation. **AgentCore:** Revokes session tokens, keeps backend secrets sealed in KMS/Secrets Manager, and tears down the isolated microVM session on completion or revocation. |
| **Evidence** | **Dynamo v1.6.0:** Versioned gRPC KV pool state relay (`#14379`), session-prefix index (`#13807`), and request/inferred tool traces (`DYN_REQUEST_TRACE=1`). **AgentCore:** CloudWatch gateway allow/deny logs, episodic memory audit trails, and 13 continuous evaluators. |
| **Chronology** | **Technical document date:** Dynamo session-aware agentic inference design published Oct 8, 2026; AWS Cedar ABAC/Gateway governance patterns documented Jun–Aug 2026. **Release date:** Dynamo v0.6.0 GA (Oct 28, 2025), Dynamo v1.0.0 GA (Mar 12, 2026), Dynamo v1.6.0 (Oct 22, 2026); AgentCore Policy GA (Mar 2026 / expanded Jun 11, 2026) & AgentCore Harness GA (Jun 2026). **Documented implementation date:** Dynamo v1.6.0 PRs `#13807`, `#14123`, `#14176`, `#14177`, `#14379`, `#14570`, `#15164` merged prior to Oct 22, 2026. **Demonstrated functional behavior date:** Post-dates both the December 19, 2024 SSPS™ filing baseline and April 15, 2025 Mint-to Logic™ drawings. |
| **Relationship** | **Partial / Analogous** on boundary deferral, gated holds, and pre-execution policy checks (`[200]`, `[400]`, `[500b]`, `[500c]`, `[500d]`); **Absent** for a sealed cryptographic **Mint Unit Container** (`[300]`) and authorization-gated single-use unit **Burn** (`[500a]`). |

