### Chart 1B: Pre-/Post-Tool Execution Interception & Two-Point Boundary Gating

| Evidence Field | Required Finding |
| --- | --- |
| **SSPS reference** | **Mint-to Logic™** (April 15, 2025 drawings, Stage `[200]` Validation/Trigger, Stage `[500c]` Access, Stage `[500d]` Code, and Stage `[600]` Audit Trail) and **The Shepherd's Method™ / Process** (December 19, 2024 baseline — pre-execution supervision and output inspection). |
| **External product** | **NVIDIA NeMo Guardrails** (`IORails` & `LLMRails` rail orchestration with Colang flows, tool allowlists, and two-point tool interception). |
| **Input** | User prompts, model-proposed `tool_call` payloads (tool name + structured arguments), and external `tool_result` return payloads. |
| **Validation** | Input rails (jailbreak/injection/topic checks), pre-execution tool allowlist and argument schema/policy validation on proposed `tool_call` payloads, and post-execution inspection/sanitization on returned `tool_result` data. |
| **State artifact** | Colang dialog/rail execution state and structured rail decision/intervention records for the active turn; does not mint a persistent portable cryptographic Mint Unit Container (`[300]`). |
| **Routing** | Deterministic Colang flow branching routes requests through ordered input rails, LLM generation, pre-tool rails, tool invocation, post-tool rails, and output rails, short-circuiting to refusal/fallback responses on rail violation. |
| **Execution** | Permits approved tool invocations to execute in the host/tool runtime while blocking or masking disallowed tool calls and unsafe tool outputs. |
| **Terminal behavior** | Returns validated response or structured refusal/block event and clears turn-scoped rail context; lacks a single-use credential/unit burn transition (`[500a]`). |
| **Evidence** | Rail execution logs, triggered rail identifiers, latency/intervention telemetry, and OpenTelemetry trace spans. |
| **Chronology** | **Technical document date:** NeMo Guardrails initial Colang/rail architecture published 2023; agentic tool-rail and `IORails` patterns expanded across 2025–2026 releases. **Release date:** Core framework released 2023; modern tool-call/tool-result rail extensions documented in 2025–2026. **Documented implementation date:** Pre-existing rail concepts (2023) extended to multi-step agentic tool boundaries post-2024. **Demonstrated functional behavior date:** Core input/output rail gating pre-dates December 19, 2024 (established baseline); agentic two-point MCP/tool-boundary governance matures in 2025–2026. |
| **Relationship** | **Partial / Analogous** on pre-execution validation and two-point tool/code boundary enforcement (`[200]`, `[500c]`, `[500d]`); **Absent** for `[300]` Mint Unit Container lifecycle, `[500a]` single-use burn, and `[500b]` timer-driven Limbo escalation/auto-burn. |

